he simplest utilities first. True and false are the most trivial (exit-code-only programs).\n\nFor weight checking: I don't have weights from requirements.yaml, but the constraint says \"Every requirement in requirements.yaml has a weight field (default 1).\" Without knowing specific weights, I'll assume weight=1 (default) and keep to 4 requirements per task.\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"cmd/true: implement true utility (srd013-true R1.1-R1.3, R2.1-R2.3)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd013-true.yaml (full SRD for true)\n      - docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml (shared_protocols section for SIGPIPE and differential testing patterns)\n      - pkg/sys/sigpipe.go (InstallSIGPIPEHandler usage pattern)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/true/main.go\n        action: create\n        note: true utility -- exits 0, supports --help and --version\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement true to exit with status 0 when invoked with no arguments (srd013-true R1.1)\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Exit with status 0 when invoked with any non-option arguments, ignoring them (srd013-true R1.2)\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Print --help output to stdout and exit 0 when --help is passed (srd013-true R1.3)\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Print --version output to stdout and exit 0 when --version is passed (srd013-true R2.1)\"\n      - id: R5\n        text: \"Call sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() at the start of main (srd013-true R2.2)\"\n      - id: R6\n        text: \"Match GNU true behavior: any single-dash flag (e.g. -x) is silently ignored and exits 0 (srd013-true R2.3)\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Call sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() at the top of main() per the shared SIGPIPE protocol\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Use os.Args directly for argument parsing -- true has no flag processing beyond --help and --version\"\n      -